{"type":"message","id":"470d2a9f","parentId":"eaf99ec9","timestamp":"2026-07-28T10:36:02.863Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-WfBvM5aJNBq4sEgZkAaMPw","toolName":"web_search","content":[{"type":"text","text":"{\n  \"query\": \"Yibin Yan \\\"StreamFormer\\\" ICCV 2025 affiliation university\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 1122,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3b553126def78664\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLearning Streaming Video Representation via Multitask Training\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"3b553126def78664\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://go2heart.github.io/streamformer/\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a47bf62827d7b3b6\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nYibin Yan*, Jilan Xu*, Shangzhe Di, Yikun Liu, Yudi Shi, Qirui Chen, Zeqian Li, Yifei Huang, Weidi Xie · School of Artificial Intelligence, <strong>Shanghai Jiao Tong University</strong> Shanghai Innovation Institute, Shanghai AI Laboratory, Fudan University ICCV 2025 Oral\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a47bf62827d7b3b6\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"go2heart.github.io\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8b732b7f5dd31204\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nLearning Streaming Video Representation via Multitask Training\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8b732b7f5dd31204\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content/ICCV2025/papers/Yan_Learning_Streaming_Video_Representation_via_Multitask_Training_ICCV_2025_paper.pdf\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5b409b44f8199dac\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nYibin Yan1,2∗, Jilan Xu3,4∗, Shangzhe Di1 , Yikun Liu1 , Yudi Shi1, Qirui Chen1 , Zeqian Li1 , Yifei Huang4 , Weidi Xie1 · 1School of Artificial Intelligence, <strong>Shanghai Jiao Tong University</strong> ... Q: Has the matador got hit? A: No. Q: Does he succeed in his performance?\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"5b409b44f8199dac\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"openaccess.thecvf.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"41c81025653ca04b\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nICCV Poster Learning Streaming Video Representation via Multitask Training\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"41c81025653ca04b\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://iccv.thecvf.com/virtual/2025/poster/2713\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a8c8d3b70031e56e\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nUnlike offline video understanding, streaming video understanding requires the ability to process video streams frame by frame, preserve historical information, and make low-latency decisions.To address these challenges, our main contributions are three-fold. (i) We develop a novel streaming video backbone, termed as StreamFormer, by incorporating causal temporal attention into a pre-trained vision transformer.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a8c8d3b70031e56e\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 22, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"iccv.thecvf.com\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fe456949c8a8204a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n[2504.20041] Learning Streaming Video Representation via Multitask Training\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"fe456949c8a8204a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/abs/2504.20041\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8e6acba06b1f9bab\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\n(iii) We conduct extensive experiments on online action detection, online video instance segmentation, and video question answering. StreamFormer achieves competitive results while maintaining efficiency, demonstrating its potential for real-time applications. From: Yibin Yan [view email] [v1] Mon, 28 Apr 2025 17:59:54 UTC (4,498 KB) [v2] Tue, 22 Jul 2025 09:34:45 UTC (10,761 KB)\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"8e6acba06b1f9bab\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"July 22, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"arxiv.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a070b19efebd29d2\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nPaper page - Learning Streaming Video Representation via Multitask Training\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a070b19efebd29d2\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://huggingface.co/papers/2504.20041\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2f7b97419f2ddb58\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nUnlike offline video understanding, streaming video understanding requires the ability to process video streams frame by frame, preserve historical information, and make low-latency decisions. To address these challenges, our main contributions are three-fold. (i) We develop a novel streaming video backbone, termed as StreamFormer, by incorporating causal temporal attention into a pre-trained vision transformer.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"2f7b97419f2ddb58\\\">>>\",\n      \"siteName\": \"huggingface.co\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}],"details":{"query":"Yibin Yan \"StreamFormer\" ICCV 2025 affiliation university","provider":"brave","count":5,"tookMs":1122,"externalContent":{"untrusted":true,"source":"web_search","provider":"brave","wrapped":true},"results":[{"title":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3b553126def78664\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nLearning Streaming Video Representation via Multitask Training\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"3b553126def78664\">>>","url":"https://go2heart.github.io/streamformer/","description":"\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a47bf62827d7b3b6\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nYibin Yan*, Jilan Xu*, Shangzhe Di, Yikun Liu, Yudi Shi, Qirui Chen, Zeqian Li, Y