{"type":"message","id":"6a8b12dd","parentId":"470d2a9f","timestamp":"2026-07-28T10:36:15.842Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Excellent! Now I have confirmed:\n\n1. **FixTalk** (paper #2881) - Shuai Tan is from **Shanghai Jiao Tong University** (confirmed from ICCV Daily)\n2. **Knowledge Distillation for Learned Image Compression** (paper #2896) - Yunuo Chen - the search result shows \"Yunuo Chen1∗ Zezheng Lyu2∗\" which suggests two affiliations. The Zhihu snippet said \"机构：上海交通大学, 麻省理工学院 等\" which means SJTU is first. But I need to verify this more carefully.\n3. **Learning Streaming Video Representation via Multitask Training** (paper #2901) - Yibin Yan is from **Shanghai Jiao Tong University** (first affiliation), with Fudan University as a secondary affiliation. The paper page says \"1School of Artificial Intelligence, Shanghai Jiao Tong University\" and the author list shows Yibin Yan with superscript 1, so SJTU is the first affiliation.\n\nNow I need to check more papers. Let me also check the ROAR paper and other candidates.\n\nWait, I also need to be careful about the \"第一单位\" definition. In Chinese academic context, \"第一单位\" typically means the first-listed affiliation of the first author. So for the StreamFormer paper, Yibin Yan's first affiliation is SJTU (School of Artificial Intelligence, Shanghai Jiao Tong University), even though there's also a Fudan University affiliation for other authors.\n\nLet me now check the remaining candidates more systematically. Let me try to access the PDF or HTML pages for the key papers to check affiliations.\n","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"text","text":"\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-3E7M9Dq3SizDAeJtUXDfMK","name":"web_search","arguments":{"count":5,"query":"Hanyi Wang \"ROAR\" ICCV 2025 watermark affiliation university"}},{"type":"text","text":"\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-bJkzsgiPMQJx9P7nVPFvzL","name":"web_search","arguments":