{"type":"message","id":"3eaefe2a","parentId":"ff0c2ba6","timestamp":"2026-07-28T10:38:50.077Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-26ftKY3rAHiAN78zxLfBoF","toolName":"exec","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== kd_compression.pdf ===\nThis ICCV paper is the Open Access version, provided by the Computer Vision Foundation.\nExcept for this watermark, it is identical to the accepted version;\nthe final published version of the proceedings is available on IEEE Xplore.\n\nKnowledge Distillation for Learned Image Compression\nYunuo Chen1∗\n\nZezheng Lyu2∗ Bing He1 Ning Cao3 Gang Chen3 Guo Lu1 B Wenjun Zhang1\n1\nShanghai Jiao Tong Unversity 2 Massachusetts Institute of Technology\n3\nE-surfing Vision Technology Co., Ltd.\n\nFigure 1. State-of-the-Art Performance of KDIC. We propose a knowledge distillation framework for learned image compression and\ndevelop KDIC, a compact and efficient student model based on S2CFormer [12]. As shown in Figure (a), KDIC outperforms recent advanced\nmethods in rate-distortion (RD) metrics and model complexity measures. Figure (b) highlights the effectiveness of knowledge distillation: it\nachieves a 2.5% reduction in BDrate while reducing parameters by 40% and FLOPs by 57% compared to the teacher model. The circle\nradius corresponds to the parameter count of each model.\n\nAbstract\n\n=== streaming_video.pdf ===\nThis ICCV paper is the Open Access version, provided by the Computer Vision Foundation.\nExcept for this watermark, it is identical to the accepted version;\nthe final published version of the proceedings is available on IEEE Xplore.\n\nLearning Streaming Video Representation via Multitask Training\nYibin Yan1,2∗ , Jilan Xu3,4∗ , Shangzhe Di1 , Yikun Liu1 , Yudi Shi1 ,\nQirui Chen1 , Zeqian Li1 , Yifei Huang4 , Weidi Xie1\n1\nSchool of Artificial Intelligence, Shanghai Jiao Tong University\n2\nShanghai Innovation Institute 3 Fudan University 4 Shanghai AI Laboratory\n\n[Online Action Detection]\n\nNo action\n\nBullfighting\n\nBullfighting\n\n\n=== roar.pdf ===\nThis ICCV paper is the Open Access version, provided by the Computer Vision Foundation.\nExcept for this watermark, it is identical to the accepted version;\nthe final published version of the proceedings is available on IEEE Xplore.\n\nROAR: Reducing Inversion Error in Generative Image Watermarking\n*\n\nHanyi Wang1 Han Fang2, Shi-Lin Wang1 Ee-Chien Chang2\n1\nShanghai Jiao Tong University 2 National University of Singapore\nwhy 820@sjtu.edu.cn, fanghan@nus.edu.sg, wsl@sjtu.edu.cn, changec@comp.nus.edu.sg\n\nAbstract\n\nEmbe\n\ndding\n\nWatermarked\nStarting Latent"}],"details":{"status":"completed","exitCode":0,"durationMs":73,"aggregated":"=== kd_compression.pdf ===\nThis ICCV paper is the Open Access version, provided by the Computer Vision Foundation.\nExcept for this watermark, it is identical to the accepted version;\nthe final published version of the proceedings is available on IEEE Xplore.\n\nKnowledge Distillation for Learned Image Compression\nYunuo Chen1∗\n\nZezheng Lyu2∗ Bing He1 Ning Cao3 Gang Chen3 Guo Lu1 B Wenjun Zhang1\n1\nShanghai Jiao Tong Unversity 2 Massachusetts Institute of Technology\n3\nE-surfing Vision Technology Co., Ltd.\n\nFigure 1. State-of-the-Art Performance of KDIC. We propose a knowledge distillation framework for learned image compression and\ndevelop KDIC, a compact and efficient student model based on S2CFormer [12]. As shown in Figure (a), KDIC outperforms recent advanced\nmethods in rate-distortion (RD) metrics and model complexity measures. Figure (b) highlights the effectiveness of knowledge distillation: it\nachieves a 2.5% reduction in BDrate while reducing parameters by 40% and FLOPs by 57% compared to the teacher model. The circle\nradius corresponds to the parameter count of each model.\n\nAbstract\n\n=== streaming_video.pdf ===\nThis ICCV paper is the Open Access version, provided by the Computer Vision Foundation.\nExcept for this watermark, it is identical to the accepted version;\nthe final published version of the proceedings is available on IEEE Xplore.\n\nLearning Streaming Video Representation via Multitask Training\nYibin Yan1,2∗ , Jilan Xu3,4∗ , Shangzhe Di1 , Yikun Liu1 , Yudi Shi1 ,\nQirui Chen1 , Zeqian Li1 , Yifei Huang4 , Weidi Xie1\n1\nSchool of Artificial Intelligence, Shanghai Jiao Tong University\n2\nShanghai Innovation Institute 3 Fudan University 4 Shanghai AI Laboratory\n\n[Online Action Detection]\n\nNo action\n\nBullfighting\n\nBullfighting\n\n\n=== roar.pdf ===\nThis ICCV paper is the Open Access version, provided by the Computer Vision Foundation.\nExcept for this watermark, it is identical to the accepted version;\nthe final published version of the proceedings is available on IEEE Xplore.\n\nROAR: Reducing Inversion Error in Generative Image Watermarking\n*\n\nHanyi Wang1 Han Fang2, Shi-Lin Wang1 Ee-Chien Chang2\n1\nShanghai Jiao Tong University 2 National University of Singapore\nwhy 820@sjtu.edu.cn, fanghan@nus.edu.sg, wsl@sjtu.edu.cn, changec@comp.nus.edu.sg\n\nAbstract\n\nEmbe\n\ndding\n\nWatermarked\nStarting Latent","cwd":"/root"},"isError":false,"timestamp":1785235130061}}
